  "description": "Two behaviours in one invocation, and they compose. First the PF13 fold: CSSTRPFY L54-55 maps DFHPF13 to CCARD-AID-PFK01, not to PFK13 - the copybook enumerates PF13 through PF24 back onto PFK01 through PFK12 - and PFK01 is not one of the two valid keys, so :298 coerces it to ENTER. Second the discard at :268-270: CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM is 'COMEN01C' and CDEMO-PGM-REENTER is false, so INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA throws away the account and card the caller sent. EIBCALEN is 172, so 1200 takes its ELSE at :461 and reads the INITIALIZEd commarea, where CDEMO-ACCT-ID and CDEMO-CARD-NUM are zero - which is why both criterion fields are LOW-VALUES rather than the caller's values.",
